{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1089442-understanding-trinkets","id":1089442,"title":"Understanding Trinkets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T16:05:31-07:00","id":1089442,"title":"Understanding Trinkets","content":"So I'm a bit fuzzy on the mechanics for how trinkets work. I understand the concept, that they're minor magical items or single-use items, but how do you craft them? How many spheres of Prime do you need? Do you need Matter? Obviously you'd need other spheres as appropriate to pull off whatever effect you want it to have, but what are the limitations of a trinket?<br /> <br /> I apologize for asking, but the M20 explanation wasn't sinking in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:10:39-07:00","id":1089500,"title":"","content":"You don't need any dots in Prime to make Trinkets. They are objects whose properties have been altered by other Spheres (usually Forces or Matter), with enough successes that their Duration is permanent.<br /> <br /> A hoodie whose materials are enhanced by Matter to resist damage. A pair of shoes that cancel sound a couple centimeters around them, so they are completely silent. A sheet of steel or a tripwire made invisible. Even a clock that has been affected by Time 3, such that it keeps absolute, perfect time. When the items have magick weaved into them so well, they become part of its base state. Though, of course, it can still be unweaved.<br /> <br /> (Yes, M20 does present the TruShades as Trinkets, despite them having an activated component like a Talisman or Device. M20 is host to a number of questionable decisions, and you should take this particular case as an exception, for the sake of simplicity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T22:41:57-07:00","id":1089588,"title":"","content":"Yes. 'trinkets' in M20 are basically non-wonders that behave like wonders. Any object that you enchant with spheres (+ duration) the normal way is a Trinket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:22:49-07:00","id":1089621,"title":"","content":"This has got me thinking about the extent of what trinkets can do and if might not be somewhat unbalanced, I would ask someone to correct me if I'm mistaken, but is this a valid RAW creation of a trinket?<br /> <br /> A gun for example, as per M20 How Do You Do That's \u201cLocked\u201d Quirks of Physics (pg. 31), &quot;Locking a Forces Effect onto a person, for instance, would also demand Life 4, while investing it into a jacket would also require Matter 2 or higher.&quot; Leading to the fair assumption Matter 3, as has been evidenced before throughout the book, is necessary to lock an effect to something with the complexity of a gun.<br /> <br /> Now at M20 Mage the Ascension, under the header Targeted Damage Effect (pg. 563) there's the following passage,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bruce Foster sights, aims, and shoots. A .44 Magnum slug<br /> tears into the raging man-beast that\u2019s been rampaging through<br /> the office complex. The monster sneers \u2013 Bullets? How pathetic<br /> \u2013 and then howls in realization that the special Technocratic<br /> ammo in Bruce\u2019s gun, combined with Bruce\u2019s Enlightened<br /> marksmanship, has unexpected, deadly consequences.<br /> \u201cThanks to our special ammo,\u201d says Bruce\u2019s player, Bill, \u201cI\u2019m<br /> using the gun to throw a coincidental Forces/ Prime Effect into<br /> that lycanthropic bastard: Forces 2 for velocity and damage, and<br /> Prime 2 to energize my bullets so they do aggravated damage.\u201d<br /> Because this is a coincidental Effect, the difficulty is 5. (2 + 3 = 5)<br /> Bill rolls Bruce\u2019s Enlightenment of 4 to trigger the desired<br /> Effect. Four dice hit the table, scoring two successes.<br /> To see whether or not the gunshot hits, Bill rolls with Bruce\u2019s<br /> Dexterity + Firearms dice pool. Three successes. Bruce\u2019s gun<br /> can fire up to three shots per turn; because a player can make<br /> only one Arete/ Enlightenment roll per turn, however, the Effect<br /> roll applies the damage to as the result of all three shots.<br /> Checking the Base Damage and Duration chart, Bill discovers<br /> that his two successes, plus one additional success for the<br /> Forces Sphere, equal six health levels\u2019 worth of damage.<br /> Because the Prime 2 addition enhanced that damage, the<br /> arrogant lupine who figured he could shake off that pistol<br /> shot suddenly takes a six health-level aggravated damage<br /> attack. Sure, the werewolf can try to soak that damage,<br /> but still \u2013 six agg in a single turn? That shit\u2019s gonna hurt.<br /> Suddenly, Wolfie\u2019s not quite as spry as he was a moment ago\u2026 </div> </div> </div>That being said, considering a mage consacretes his bullets with Prime 2 priorly in order for them to deal aggravated damage (adding Duration, naturally), and that he locks a Forces 2 effect with Matter 3 to the gun, with for example, three successes for damage (totalling 4 because of +1 innate to the Forces Sphere), and appropriate successes for Duration, would that leave him with a gun that deals eight health levels of aggravated every time it is shot until the Duration expires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","user":"Rotwood","date":". 05-08-2017, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:53:14-07:00","id":1089815,"title":"","content":"Okay, thanks for clearing that up everyone. I guess I got trinkets and charms mixed up when they were mentioned in How Do You Do That? on page","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}